%% DM26-0670

%% A client publishes on a topic, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/cassini-broker.md "Policy in the broker" and
%% "The bounds, as built"). What happens before the wire is general/cassini_client_publish, and what happens when there is
%% no room is broker/backpressure_admission.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Agent (facade and transport)
    participant Reader as the connection's reader
    participant Listener
    participant Session as SessionAgent
    participant Broker
    participant Topic as TopicManager / TopicAgent
    participant Sub as SubscriberAgent
    participant Peer as each subscriber's Listener

    Client->>Reader: PublishRequest(registration_id, topic, payload, share_identity, epoch and seq)
    Reader->>Reader: admit it: the connection's window, then the memory budget<br/>(a charge that travels with the payload)
    Reader->>Listener: PublishRequest, stamped published_by and published_instance from the connection
    alt no session on this connection, or another session's id
        Listener-->>Client: ErrorMessage("Bad request: ...")
    else not yet bound to its session
        Listener-->>Client: PublishResponse(Err, Unavailable, origin)
        Note over Client: Refused for now: a facade keeps it and sends it again.
    else Listener::decide: Cedar first, then the floor from the certificate, default deny
        Listener-->>Client: PublishResponse(Err reason, Denied, origin)
        Client->>Client: the entry is settled, ClientEvent::PublishRefused
    else allowed
        opt the topic carries authority, from the identity that may publish it
            Listener->>Listener: the broker hears it itself (BrokerAuthority::hear)
        end
        Listener->>Session: PublishRequest(topic, payload, published_by, id, window)
        Session->>Broker: PublishRequest
        Broker->>Topic: PublishRequest (a topic is created on first use)
        Note over Topic: It waits here, in order, holding its connection's window,<br/>while a subscriber above its high water holds the topic back.
        alt the topic has subscribers
            Topic->>Sub: PublishResponse(topic, payload, published_by, published_instance, origin)
            Sub->>Sub: number it, hold it in the delivery outbox until it is acknowledged
            Sub->>Peer: PushMessage(delivery_id)
            Topic-->>Session: PublishRequestAck(id)
            Session-->>Client: PublishRequestAck(topic, id)
            Client->>Client: exactly that entry leaves the outbox,<br/>ClientEvent::PublishAcknowledged
        else no subscribers, and the budget allows
            Topic->>Topic: queue it for the first subscriber (dropped by age after 180 s)
            Topic-->>Session: PublishRequestAck(id)
            Session-->>Client: PublishRequestAck(topic, id)
        else no subscribers, and the budget is exhausted
            Topic-->>Session: PublishResponse(Err, Unavailable, origin)
            Session-->>Client: PublishResponse(Err, Unavailable, origin)
        end
    end
    Note over Topic,Client: The acknowledgement is acceptance, not delivery, and is per message, in no particular order.
